.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-DEMO-PUBLISH 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-demo-publish
.Nd open the demo to browsers on the network, from this host's LAN address
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -port Ar n
.Nm
.Fl -status | -off
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The demo's address comes from MetalLB, on the cluster's own network,
which on a single kldload host sits behind libvirt: reachable from the
host and nowhere else, and on most machines the same 192.168.122.0/24 a
visitor's own laptop uses.
.Nm
reads the address the demo's
.Ql web
Service was given and forwards a port on the host's LAN address to it,
with a systemd socket and
.Xr systemd-socket-proxyd 8 ,
which every distribution here has.
It then fetches the page through the LAN address, as a browser would, and
prints the address to open only when that returns 200.
.Pp
The Service's address is written into the unit; run it again after the
Service is recreated.
Running it again is safe.
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -port Ar n
The port to listen on; default 8088.
.It Fl -status
Whether the forwarder is running, and where it forwards.
.It Fl -off
Stop and remove the forwarder.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NS
The demo's namespace; default
.Ql demo .
.It Ev KUBECONFIG
Default
.Pa /root/.kube/config .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/systemd/system/kldload-demo-publish.socket , Pa .service
The forwarder.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the page answered through the LAN address, or for
.Fl -status
and
.Fl -off ;
1 when the Service has no address or the page did not answer; 2 when
the port is not a port.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop with no demo, on 2026-09-30, with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-demo-publish --status
inactive
# (exited 0)
$ kube-demo-publish --port 70000
kube-demo-publish: --port needs a port number, 1-65535: 70000
# (exited 2)
$ kube-demo-publish --frob
FATAL: unknown argument: --frob (try --help)
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
Publishing; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-demo-publish --port 9000
# prints the address to open once the page has answered through it
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr systemd.socket 5 ,
.Xr kube-demo 8 ,
.Xr kube-demo-image 8 ,
.Xr systemd-socket-proxyd 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: the port and the Service's address went
into the unit files unchecked.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
It listens on every address of the host, not only the LAN one.
